        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> I rewrite it in my local machine as belows:\r\n> \r\n> ```lua\r\n> local origin = MiniStatusline.is_truncated\r\n> ---@diagnostic disable-next-line: duplicate-set-field\r\n> function MiniStatusline.is_truncated(trunc_width)\r\n>   if vim.o.laststatus == 3 then return vim.o.columns < (trunc_width or -1) end\r\n>   return origin(trunc_width)\r\n> end\r\n> ```\r\n\r\nOf course, updating `is_truncated()` is a most straightforward solution. But it implies that checking for `laststatus = 3` is done for every section which is suboptimal. Not sure if squeezing this optimization would be worth it, but I'll look into it.\r\n\r\nThis is a more streamlined version:\r\n```lua\r\nMiniStatusline.is_truncated = function(trunc_width)\r\n  -- Use -1 to default to 'not truncated'\r\n  local cur_width = vim.o.laststatus == 3 and vim.o.columns or vim.api.nvim_win_get_width(0)\r\n  return cur_width < (trunc_width or -1)\r\nend\r\n```\r\n\r\nI'll look into it soon.",
            "created_at": "2023-02-06T10:03:48Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/218#issuecomment-1418819100",
